This patch is needed because `fslock` uses `flock(2)` by default, while the
Solaris build uses `fcntl(2)`-style advisory locking instead.

What it does:
- adds a Solaris/Illumos-specific helper using `fcntl`
- switches `lock`, `try_lock`, and `unlock` to that implementation
- keeps the existing `flock` behavior on other Unix targets

Why it is needed:
- without it, the `v8-solaris` crate cannot use the vendored `fslock` crate
  correctly on Solaris

--- a/v8-147.4.0-vendored-sources/fslock/src/unix.rs
